scanner.c: no automatic semicolon before a same-line word starting with `e`, which cut
`return emit(x)` into `return` and `emit(x)`. packages/syntechs/src/grammars/kotlin/scanner.ts ports the
same change. grammar.js: `fun interface`, an enum body's repeated `;`, and an `=` in an if/when/while
condition (which ktfmt formats although the compiler rejects it), and an annotated declaration winning over
an annotated expression when both parse.

